📖 Overview

This project focused on footprinting and Open-Source Intelligence (OSINT) using Maltego, a graphical link-analysis and reconnaissance tool.

The practical involved configuring Maltego, creating a domain-based graph, and using a search-engine-based transform to identify publicly discoverable email information associated with "networkwalks.com".

The exercise provided hands-on experience with the reconnaissance phase of a security assessment and demonstrated how publicly available information can contribute to an organization's external footprint.

«⚠️ Disclaimer: This activity was performed strictly for educational purposes within an authorized training environment.»

